From: QED64 Toolchain <qed64-toolchain@localhost>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 11:51:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/20] feat: host-pumped LSP file worker entry points

This PR adds lean_wasm_lsp_init and lean_wasm_lsp_send, letting an embedder that cannot provide a blocking stdin (WASM hosts must keep their event loop live for cross-thread proxying) drive a single-file language-server session one JSON-RPC message at a time: init replicates the watchdog's initialize/didOpen startup sequence of initAndRunWorker, send runs one mainLoop dispatch for an already-read message, and server-to-client traffic flows through the worker's ordinary stdout channel. The report delay is forced to 0: timed sleeps on dedicated pthreads do not wake under this Emscripten build, and the reporter's first statement is that sleep.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
